# Mode Responses — Always Active

Follow the section for the current Cursor mode. Do not mix them.

## Ask mode

Every reply uses short, easy English.

- Short words. Short sentences. One idea per sentence.
- Say what it means for the user first. File paths and jargon only if they need them.
- Explain, do not implement.
- Do not dump long code unless they asked for it.

```text
❌ The RPC list_shop_price_overrides is a SECURITY DEFINER function that
   joins global_stock_allocations under RLS.

✅ This page loads prices from a server function. It only shows stock
   that this shop is allowed to sell.
```

## Agent mode

If blocked because the docs do not state a needed fact, do **not** reply `Done`. Reply with the `DOC_GAP` block from `.cursor/rules/docs-first.mdc` and stop.

When the task is finished, reply with exactly:

Done

Add 1–2 sentences only if the user must know something important:

- they need to restart, migrate, or run a command
- something is blocked or risky
- a choice was made that changes later work

Do not recap files, diffs, or steps. Do not list what you changed.

```text
❌ Updated ShopPricingPage.vue to debounce search and wired the store.

✅ Done
   Restart the dev server so the new env var is picked up.
```

## Plan mode

Use this **section order** every time. Do not implement in plan mode.

### 1 — Plan

One short title: what we are building or fixing.

### 2 — Overview

Plain outcome in a few bullets:

- What the user can do when done
- Scope in / out (one line each if needed)
- Docs to read first (`spec.md`, `00-gaps.md`, …)
- Blockers or dependencies on other work

### 3 — Frontend changes

Summary of **all** web work (not phased yet). List paths under `web/`:

- Pages, routes, nav
- Components, composables, stores/services/repositories
- Types, query keys, user-visible behavior

Tables or bullets. Name symbols when it matters. No step-by-step implementation here — that goes in phases.

### 4 — Backend changes

Summary of **all** Supabase work (not phased yet). List paths under `supabase/`:

- Schema files, migrations (new file names only — bodies live in schemas first per project rules)
- RPCs, tables, RLS, tests under `supabase/tests/`

Same rule: inventory and intent here; detailed edits in phases.

### 5 — Phases

Slice implementation here. **Phase 1** is the first shippable slice. Later phases depend on earlier ones when they must.

For **every** phase write:

- **Goal** — what this phase delivers
- **Files** — exact paths to create, edit, or delete
- **Change** — what to add, edit, or remove in each file (symbol names, behavior, not “update the store”)

Phase rules:

- Name files and functions. Paste key signatures or field names when they matter.
- If you looked something up, put the finding in the phase (implement must not re-research).
- Frontend/backend sections are the map; phases are the execution order (a phase may touch only FE, only BE, or both).
- Stop after the last phase.

```text
## Plan
Shop pricing search debounce

## Overview
- Search waits before hitting the server so typing does not spam requests.
- In: Shop pricing list search. Out: other shop pages.
- Read: docs/features/shop_order/spec.md

## Frontend changes
- web/src/modules/shop_order/pages/ShopPricingPage.vue — debounce onSearchInput

## Backend changes
- (none)

## Phases

Phase 1 — Add debounce to shop pricing search
Goal: Typing in search waits 300ms before fetching.
Files:
- web/src/modules/shop_order/pages/ShopPricingPage.vue
Change:
- In onSearchInput, wrap shopPricingStore.loadList() with a 300ms
  debounce. Reuse existing searchQuery ref. Do not add a new composable.
```
